## Activation choice (stated per task)
Activation is a DIRECT TRANSACTIONAL API CALL (POST /api/v1/sources/{id}/activate) on already-existing artifacts (parsed source version + canonical document). No job is driven from the API; the API only enqueued the parse job at acquisition (T12), and the live worker owns that job's lifecycle to the `parsed` state. ch05: "Service logic plus serializable/advisory-lock sections protect cross-row rules such as ... active-version swap" — the swap runs as one transaction guarded by source-row FOR UPDATE locks plus the partial unique index uq_source_versions_one_active (double win impossible).

