## Pre-fix / post-fix swap-order probe (empirical, on the T13 scratch)
- probe-swap-order.sql (pre-fix order: promote new active BEFORE demoting the old active, one transaction):
  ERROR: duplicate key value violates unique constraint "uq_source_versions_one_active" — DETAIL: Key (source_id)=(00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000003) already exists.
- probe-swap-order-fixed.sql (post-fix order: demote before promote):
  v1 -> inactive, v2 -> active, transaction commits.
- The prior WIP used the pre-fix order; every refresh (second activation) would have 500'd on the UniqueViolation. Fixed in pg_source_activation.py.

## Scenario coverage
1. upload text (paste) + PDF (import fixture.pdf) -> live worker w14 parses both (jobs succeeded)
2. Source Guide before activation -> explicit 409 problem (source_guide_unavailable)
3. activate text -> 200 (full source payload, pipeline_status=active); guide -> summary + labels ["plain text","active","canonical"]
4. activate PDF -> 200; guide -> summary + labels ["pdf","active","canonical"]
5. provenance edges written on activation: contains, derived_from, generated_from (transform identity recorded)
6. two concurrent activations on the same source -> exactly [200, 409]
7. simulated failure (newest version parsed but no canonical document) -> activation 409 source_activation_conflict; prior active version + its active canonical document + sources.current_version_id all intact; guide still 200 on the prior version
8. activated SourceVersion content tamper attempt -> RAISE (milpbooklm: activated source version ... is immutable)
9. audit_events contains source.activated rows for the 4 successful activations
